course: dictionary
lesson: 4982
title: Indent: the small gap that starts a line
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When you start a new paragraph, you often leave a small space at the start of the first line. That space is called an indent, and to indent means to start a line a little way in. «A new paragraph is shown by an indent (a small gap at the start of the line) or by a blank line; schools and books use one or the other.»
explain: The sentence gives you the clue: an indent is a small gap at the start of the line. Swap that meaning in and read it again: "A new paragraph is shown by a small gap at the start of the line" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: The same word can be a verb or a noun. You indent a line (verb), and the indent is the space itself (noun). Programmers also indent lines of code with spaces or tabs to show how the parts are grouped.
fact: To indent means to start a line a little way in from the margin.
fact: An indent is the space at the start of a line.
fact: Paragraphs are often shown by an indent or by a blank line; schools and books use one or the other.
fact: An indent can also be a small dent or notch in something.
fact: In Python, indentation is part of the rules, so the spaces at the start of a line really matter.
exercise: In a book, what is the small gap at the start of a line called? | A margin | *An indent | A heading | A blank line
exercise: «A new paragraph is shown by an indent or by a blank line.» What does indent mean here? | *A small gap at the start of the line | A word in bold | A long line at the bottom of the page | A picture
exercise: In «Please indent the first line of your story», which word is the verb, the action you must do? | line | story | *indent | first
test: Maya says an indent is a type of dent in a car. What is the best answer? | *Partly right: a dent is one meaning, but in writing an indent is a gap at the start of a line | No, an indent is a colour | Yes, and it is always in a car | No, an indent is only a dent in metal
test: What does an indented coastline have? | *Many bays and inlets | Waves made of ice | Only one sandy beach | Straight sides and no bays
exam: In Python, why does indentation matter? | It stops the computer from running the code | *It is part of the rules, so the spaces show how the code is grouped | It means the code is finished | It only makes the code look neater and changes nothing
